In providing an introduction to computer science (using Python), - Daniel
Lim presents in this book key philosophical issues, ranging from external
world skepticism to the existence of God to the problem of induction.
These issues, and others, are introduced through the use of critical com-
putational concepts, ranging from image manipulation to recursive pro-
